                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} O(n)
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%E2%88%9E-action"} ∞-action
              on
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi Corr
                      %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn ∞
                    %mi Grpd
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Corr_n(\infty Grpd)
              induced via prop.
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#CorrnGrpdHasDuals"}
              by the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cobordism+hypothesis"} cobordism hypothesis
              (see there at
              = succeed ")" do
                %em
                  %a{:href => "cobordism+hypothesis#TheCanonicalOnAction"} the canonical O(n)-action
          %p
            This statement appears in (
            %a{:href => "#Lurie"}> Lurie, below remark 3.2.3
            ) without formal proof. For more see (
            %a{:href => "#Haugseng14"}> Haugseng 14, remark 9.7
            ).
          %p More generally:
          .num_prop
            %h6#proposition_3 Proposition
            %p
              For
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi H
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{H}
              an
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-topos"} (∞,1)-topos
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi Corr
                      %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi H
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
