            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sheaf+with+transfer"}> sheaf with transfer
                ,
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Mackey+functor"} Mackey functor
          %h2#references References
          %p
            For references on 1- and 2-categories of spans see at
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/correspondences"} correspondences
          %p
            An explicit definition of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C2%29-category"} (∞,2)-category
            of spans in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%E2%88%9EGrpd"} ∞Grpd
            is in section 10 of
          %ul
            %li#DyckerhoffKapranov12
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Tobias+Dyckerhoff"}> Tobias Dyckerhoff
              ,
              = succeed ":" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Mikhail+Kapranov"} Mikhail Kapranov
              = succeed "," do
                %em Higher Segal spaces I
              = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/1212.3563"} arxiv:1212.3563
          %p
            An inductive definition of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/symmetric+monoidal+%28%E2%88%9E%2Cn%29-category"} symmetric monoidal (∞,n)-category
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi Span
                    %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mn ∞
                  %mi Grpd
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Span_n(\infty Grpd)/C
            of spans of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%E2%88%9E-groupoid"} ∞-groupoid
            over a symmetric monoidal
            = succeed "-category" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn ∞
                    %mo ,
                    %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\infty,n)
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            is sketched in section 3.2 of
          %ul
            %li#Lurie
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jacob+Lurie"}> Jacob Lurie
              \:
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/On+the+Classification+of+Topological+Field+Theories"} On the Classification of Topological Field Theories
          %p
            there denoted
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi Fam
                      %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Fam_n(C)
          %p More detailed discussion is given in
          %ul
            %li#Haugseng14
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Rune+Haugseng"}> Rune Haugseng
                \:
                %em Iterated spans and “classical” topological field theories
                (
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/1409.0837"}> arXiv:1409.0837
                )
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Yonatan+Harpaz"}> Yonatan Harpaz
                ,
                %em Ambidexterity and the universality of finite spans
                (
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1703.09764"}> arXiv:1703.09764
                )
          %p
            Both articles comment on the relation to
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/schreiber/show/Local+prequantum+field+theory"} Local prequantum field theory
          %p
            The generalization to an
            = succeed "-category" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn ∞
                    %mo ,
                    %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\infty,n)
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi Span
                    %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mn ∞
                  %mo ,
                  %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %msup
                    %mi Cat
                    %mi Adj
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Span_n((\infty,1)Cat^Adj)
            of spans between
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cobordism+hypothesis"} (∞,n)-categories with duals
            is discussed on p. 107 and 108.
          %p
            The extension to the case when the ambient
            = succeed "-topos" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn ∞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \infty
          %ul
            %li#LiBland15
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/David+Li-Bland"}> David Li-Bland
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em The stack of higher internal categories and stacks of iterated spans
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/1506.08870"} arXiv:1506.08870
          %p
            The application of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi Span
                    %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mn ∞
                  %mi Grpd
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %mi C
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Span_n(\infty Grpd/C)
            to the construction of
            = succeed "s" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/FQFT"} FQFT
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Dan+Freed"}> Dan Freed
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Mike+Hopkins"} Mike Hopkins
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jacob+Lurie"} Jacob Lurie
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Constantin+Teleman"} Constantin Teleman
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Topological+Quantum+Field+Theories+from+Compact+Lie+Groups"} Topological Quantum Field Theories from Compact Lie Groups
          %p
            Discussion of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi Span
                    %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi H
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ≃
                  %msub
                    %mi Alg
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi E
                        %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msup
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi H
                    %mi op
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Span_n(\mathbf{H}) \simeq Alg_{E_n}(\mathbf{H}^{op})
            is around remark 2.9 of
          %ul
            %li#BenZviNadler13
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/David+Ben-Zvi"}> David Ben-Zvi
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/David+Nadler"} David Nadler
              %em Nonlinear traces
              (
              %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/1305.7175"}> arXiv:1305.7175
              )
          %p Further discussion:
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Germ%C3%A1n+Stefanich"}> Germán Stefanich
              \:
              %em Higher sheaf theory I: Correspondences
              \&amp;lbrack;
              %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/2011.03027"}> arXiv:2011.03027
              \&amp;rbrack;
          %p
            A discussion of a version
            = succeed "for" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Span
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi B
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Span(B)
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi B
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B
            a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/2-category"} 2-category
            with
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Span
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi B
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Span(B)
            regarded as a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tricategory"} tricategory
            and then as a 1-object
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tetracategory"} tetracategory
            is in
          %ul
            %li#Hoffnung
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Alex+Hoffnung"}> Alex Hoffnung
              ,
              %em Spans in 2-Categories: A monoidal tricategory
              (
              %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/1112.0560"}> arXiv:1112.0560
              )
          %p
            and for
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi B
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B
            satisfying further conditions, such as having only invertible
            = succeed "-morphisms," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn 2
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 2
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Paul+Balmer"}> Paul Balmer
              ,
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ivo+Dell%27Ambrogio"} Ivo Dell'Ambrogio
              = succeed "." do
                %em Mackey 2-functors and Mackey 2-motives
              = succeed ")." do
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1808.04902"} arXiv:1808.04902
          %p
            A discussion that
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi Span
                    %mn 2
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Span_2(-)
            in a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/2-category"} 2-category
            with weak
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/finite+limits"} finite limits
            is a
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/compact+closed+2-category"} compact closed 2-category
          %ul
            %li#Stay13
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Mike+Stay"}> Mike Stay
              ,
              %em Compact Closed Bicategories
              (
              %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/1301.1053"}> arXiv:1301.1053
              )
          %p See also
          %ul
            %li#ayalaFrancis17
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/David+Ayala"}> David Ayala
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/John+Francis"} John Francis
              %em
                Fibrations of
                = succeed "-Categories" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mn ∞
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \infty
              (
              %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1702.02681"}> arXiv:1702.02681
              )
          %p Coisotropic orrespondences for derived Poisson stacks:
          %ul
            %li#HMS19
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Rune+Haugseng"}> Rune Haugseng
              , Valerio Melani,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Pavel+Safronov"} Pavel Safronov
              %em Shifted Coisotropic Correspondences
              (
              %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1904.11312"}> arXiv:1904.11312
              )
        .revisedby
